# {{projectName}}

<!-- IF frontend=embedded -->
A full-stack application with a React/TypeScript frontend and a <!-- IF language=kotlin -->Kotlin<!-- END language --><!-- IF language=java -->Java<!-- END language -->/Spring Boot backend. One `mvn package` produces a fat JAR that serves both the API and the SPA.
<!-- END frontend -->
<!-- IF frontend=standalone -->
A <!-- IF language=kotlin -->Kotlin<!-- END language --><!-- IF language=java -->Java<!-- END language -->/Spring Boot backend and a separately deployed React/TypeScript frontend. `mvn package` produces the backend JAR; the frontend builds to static files for its own host.
<!-- END frontend -->
<!-- IF frontend=none -->
A <!-- IF language=kotlin -->Kotlin<!-- END language --><!-- IF language=java -->Java<!-- END language -->/Spring Boot backend service. `mvn package` produces a runnable JAR.
<!-- END frontend -->

Built on the [Trustworks Essentials](https://github.com/trustworksdk/essentials-project) framework.

## Architecture

<!-- IF frontend=embedded -->
```
LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
-----------------
Browser :5173  -->  Vite Dev Server (HMR)  -->  /api/*  -->  Spring Boot :8080

PRODUCTION
----------
Browser  -->  Spring Boot :8080  -->  /api/*   (API)
                                 -->  /*       (SPA static files)
                                 -->  /swagger-ui.html (API docs)
```
<!-- END frontend -->
<!-- IF frontend=standalone -->
```
LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
-----------------
Browser :5173  -->  Vite Dev Server (HMR)  -->  /api/*  -->  Spring Boot :8080

PRODUCTION
----------
Browser  -->  static host / CDN        (SPA, with its own deep-link rewrite)
Browser  -->  Spring Boot :8080 /api/* (API, cross-origin: CORS allows the SPA's origin)
```
<!-- END frontend -->
<!-- IF frontend=none -->
```
Browser / Client  -->  Spring Boot :8080  -->  /api/*       (API)
                                          -->  /v3/api-docs (OpenAPI spec)
                                          -->  /swagger-ui.html (interactive docs)
                                          -->  /actuator    (health/metrics)
```
<!-- END frontend -->

The backend is organised by **vertical slice** within bounded contexts, not by technical layer. Each bounded context gets its own package; `/essentials:add-slice` creates them.

