### Slice-manifest lint gate

Nothing in the Maven build reads `slice.yaml`, so a broken manifest compiles and ships while the slice drops out of every tool that reads manifests. `scripts/slice-lint.py` (with its schema beside it) is the gate; run it in CI from this directory:

```bash
uv run --script scripts/slice-lint.py . --schema scripts/slice-yaml.schema.json   # or python3 with pyyaml and jsonschema installed
```

Exit 0 is clean, 1 is findings, 2 is that it could not validate (a missing `jsonschema` included) — fail the build on anything but 0.
<!-- END lintGate -->
<!-- IF lintGate=hook -->

`.githooks/pre-commit` runs the same check on every commit that stages a `slice.yaml` in this project. Git never activates a hook from a clone, so **every clone runs this once**, from this directory:

```bash
git config core.hooksPath "$(git rev-parse --show-prefix).githooks"
```

If the repository already sets `core.hooksPath` (a hook manager such as husky), or `.git/hooks` holds any hook other than a `*.sample` (another tool's `post-commit` or `post-checkout` counts), do not run that: `core.hooksPath` replaces every hook in `.git/hooks`, and those hooks would silently stop running. Call this project's hook from the existing pre-commit hook instead, where `<prefix>` is what `git rev-parse --show-prefix` prints in this directory (empty at the repository root):

```bash
"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/<prefix>.githooks/pre-commit" || exit 1
```
<!-- END lintGate -->

